# 8. CATEGORY MANAGER TARGET DETECTION

A Category Manager row should be considered for Sub-Category completion when:

* Column B / Sub-Category is blank or `NA`

AND

the row otherwise contains meaningful Category Manager information, such as:

* a valid Category in column A,
* one or more Product columns,
* or other evidence showing that this is a real taxonomy row rather than an unused blank row.

Completely empty worksheet rows must not be sent to Ollama.

---

# 9. CATEGORY MANAGER DETERMINISTIC COMPLETION FIRST

Before Ollama, attempt deterministic resolution from existing ShopGraph taxonomy data.

Examples:

* existing Product/Common Name → Sub-Category mappings
* existing Category Manager rows containing the same products
* Purchase History Common Name → Sub-Category mappings
* other unambiguous existing taxonomy relationships

Only reuse a mapping when it is unambiguous.

Conflicting mappings must be sent to Ollama instead of arbitrarily selecting one.

---

